---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site, adsEnabled, analyticsEnabled } from '../config/site';
const hasAnalytics = analyticsEnabled || Boolean(site.googleAnalyticsId);
const who = site.businessName ?? 'the operator of Prunest';
---
<Page title="Privacy — Prunest" description="What Prunest stores on your device, what it does not collect, and how to delete saved plans." path="/privacy" heading="Privacy">
  <p>This page describes what this website actually does. Prunest is operated by {who}.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are no accounts and no sign-in.</li>
    <li>The measurements, prices and dates you type into the calculators are processed in your browser and are not sent to Prunest.</li>
    <li>Calculator features work without cookies.</li>
    {!adsEnabled && <li>There is no advertising on the site at present.</li>}
    {!hasAnalytics && <li>There are no analytics or tracking scripts on the site at present.</li>}
  </ul>

  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>The calculators use your browser’s local storage for these features:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your unit preference.</strong> When you switch between imperial and metric, that choice is remembered (key <code>prunest:units</code>) so other calculators open in the same units.</li>
    <li><strong>Saved plans.</strong> Only if you press “Save on this device”, the entries for that calculator are stored (keys beginning <code>prunest:plan:</code>).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This data stays in your browser on that device. It is not uploaded, and Prunest cannot see it. To remove it, press “Delete saved plan” on the calculator, or clear site data for prunest.com in your browser settings, which removes the unit preference as well.</p>
  {site.googleAnalyticsId && <p>The site also stores your analytics choice in local storage under <code>prunest:analytics</code>.</p>}
  <p>The calendar file from the seed starting calculator and any PDF you print are created on your device.</p>

  <h2>Offline copy of the site</h2>
  <p>So the calculators keep working in the garden without a signal, your browser saves a copy of Prunest’s own pages, scripts, styles and fonts in its cache storage after your first visit. The copy contains no measurements, dates or other entries, and nothing is sent anywhere because of it. It is replaced when the site is updated. Clearing site data for prunest.com in your browser settings removes it.</p>

  <h2>Links to a plan</h2>
  <p>“Copy link to this plan” builds a link with your entries encoded after the <code>#</code> in the address. Browsers do not send that part of an address to the server, so Prunest does not receive it. Anyone you give the link to can read the entries in it, so share it only with people you want to see the plan.</p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>The site is a set of static files served by Cloudflare. As with any website, when your browser requests a page, Cloudflare processes technical information such as your IP address, browser type and the page requested, in order to deliver the page and protect the service from abuse. Prunest does not run its own server or database and does not combine this information with anything you enter in the calculators.</p>

  {hasAnalytics && (
    <>
      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
      {analyticsEnabled && <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics counts page views and measures page speed without using cookies or local storage.</p>}
      {site.googleAnalyticsId && (
        <p>With your permission, Google Analytics uses cookies to measure visits. It receives page paths and technical information about your browser. Calculator entries and the query string and fragment of the page address are excluded. You can change your choice under “Analytics preferences” in the footer. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
      )}
    </>
  )}

  {adsEnabled && (
    <>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      {site.adsenseClient && (
        <p>The site shows adverts through Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve and measure adverts, including adverts based on your earlier visits to this and other websites. You can read how Google uses information at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a> and manage personalised advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>. Where the law requires consent, Google’s consent prompt is shown before personalised adverts are used.</p>
      )}
      {site.adsPortalScript && <p>The site shows its own promotional placements, loaded from a script operated for Prunest. They are labelled “Advertisement”.</p>}
      <p>Adverts are never placed among calculator inputs or results and are removed from printed plans. Calculator entries are not shared with advertisers.</p>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Prunest is a general-audience site and does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>If the site starts to use {adsEnabled ? '' : 'advertising, '}{hasAnalytics ? '' : 'analytics, '}or any new storage, this page will be updated to say so. {site.contactEmail ? <>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</> : <>See the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for how to get in touch.</>}</p>
</Page>
